let __v_168 = Value::from("Rat and mouse bait is a poison by design, so the box is the answer: a lockable bait station fixed down or pushed tight against a wall, with the block inside it and nothing loose under a cupboard. A toddler can open a screw-top tub, and a dog can chew a station pushed behind a bin, so put them where an adult can reach and a child cannot see. The poison thins the blood, so the hospital gives the antidote rather than waiting for symptoms - say what it was and when.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_BAIT", __v_168.clone())?;
let __v_169 = Value::from("Slug pellets are the garden poison a child picks up, because they are small, blue and the size of a sweet: a handful is an A&E trip, and a dog that eats them starts shaking within hours. Use them inside a closed trap or under a slate rather than scattered on a bed, or skip the poison altogether - a beer trap sunk to the rim, copper tape round a pot and nematodes watered on in spring all work.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_PELLETS", __v_169.clone())?;
let __v_170 = Value::from("Ant powder is an insecticide for cracks, not for floors: puff it along the skirting, under the worktop edge and into the gap by the pipe, leave it a week, then hoover it up. A crawling baby and a cat that licks its fur are both in the way of a dusting across a doorway, so keep the room empty until it has settled and wipe anything that was out on the side.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_POWDER", __v_170.clone())?;
let __v_171 = Value::from("Weedkiller is safe to the household when it is dry and not before: an hour on a warm day, and the lawn is a no-go for a toddler and a cat until then. Mix it outside, keep it in its own labelled bottle - never a drinks bottle, which is how most of these cases start - and let somebody else spray it if you are pregnant.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_SPRAY", __v_171.clone())?;
let __v_172 = Value::from("A trap belongs in a box or behind a unit, not on a floor a child crawls on: a snap trap at the back of a cupboard behind the kickboard, or a tunnel trap whose openings are too small for fingers. Put it where you can see it and a toddler cannot reach, check it daily, and use a live trap if there is a cat about.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_TRAP", __v_172.clone())?;
let __v_173 = Value::from("Bleach, oven cleaner and white spirit are safe in the house as long as nobody small can get at them, so the catch on the cupboard is the whole answer: the bottle they came in, the lid on tight, and never decanted into a drinks bottle or a jam jar. Gloves and an open window for the fumes, and wash the skin with plenty of water if it splashes.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_CLEANER", __v_173.clone())?;
let __v_174 = Value::from("An oil diffuser is the one to think about, because the oil is concentrated, smells of sweets and a toddler can drink a whole bottle of it. Keep reed diffusers, plug-ins and the refill bottles above arm's reach or in a locked cupboard, and use a wall plug-in rather than a bowl of oil on a side table.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_AIR", __v_174.clone())?;
let __v_175 = Value::from("Fumes are the thing with a spray, so open a window and keep the cat, the dog and the baby out of the room until it has settled, and take a fish tank or a bird out of the house altogether. Cats are the ones to be strict about: permethrin and the other pyrethroids in fly sprays and in every dog flea spray are deadly to them, so never use a dog product near a cat and keep them apart for a couple of days. A puppy and a crawling baby come next, because both lick surfaces - wipe the sides down and put the food bowls away first. A cat that starts drooling, twitching or walking wobbly after a spray needs the vet now, not tomorrow.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_AEROSOL", __v_175.clone())?;
let __v_176 = Value::from("A fogger leaves insecticide on every surface a baby touches, so the room has to be empty for the hours on the tin, with the fish tank covered, and everything washed down afterwards. With a crawling baby or a cat in the house, a spot-on treatment and a hot wash of the bedding does the same job with the poison kept on the animal.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_FOGGER", __v_176.clone())?;
let __v_177 = Value::from("Antifreeze is the sweet one and a spoonful is enough to kill a cat: it lives in a sealed container, spills are soaked up with cat litter and swept, and the bottle never sits open in the garage. A pet that has licked a spill needs the vet the same day, because the treatment works best in the first hours.");
frame.store("_CHEMICAL_ANTIFREEZE", __v_177.clone())?;
