let __v_854 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"kettle\",\"boils\",\"boil\"]},\"A kettle that switches off before it boils is scaled, and the scale is what the cut-out reads: fill it to the line with half water and half white vinegar, boil, leave it an hour and rinse. Do that once a month in a hard water area.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"microwave\"]},\"A microwave that quits part way is protecting itself from heat: clear the vents, give it 5cm of space on every side, don't run it empty, and stop using it if the turntable is not turning. One that stops after a minute on full power wants replacing, not repairing.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dishwasher\"]},\"A dishwasher that stops part way is nearly always the drain or the door: clean the filter in the base, check the hose is not kinked, and make sure the door latch clicks. A flashing tap symbol means it is not filling, so check the water is on at the valve under the sink.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"washing machine\",\"washer\",\"spin\",\"drum\"]},\"A washer that stops mid-cycle is usually the door not quite latched or a drain that cannot empty: check the door clicks shut, clean the filter behind the kick plate, look for a kinked hose. The error code names it - E20 or F21 is a draining fault on most machines.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"toaster\",\"toast\",\"pops\",\"popping\",\"pop up\"]},\"A toaster that pops early usually has a full crumb tray or a weak timer: unplug it, empty the tray, turn the dial up one notch (most count darker to the right). If it pops after a couple of seconds on every setting the latch is worn, and a new one is cheaper.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dryer\",\"tumble dryer\",\"tumble\"]},\"A dryer that cuts out is overheating: empty the lint filter after every load, clear the condenser and check the vent is not crushed, because a blocked vent is also a fire risk. If it stops with the clothes still wet on a low setting, the thermostat is the likely part.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"oven\"]},\"An oven that cuts out is usually the thermostat or the cooling fan: if it cooks unevenly or the fan is noisy before it stops, that is the fan; if it just goes cold and comes back, it is the thermostat. Both are repair jobs rather than a new oven.\"]}]}")?;
frame.store("CUTTING_OUT", __v_854.clone())?;
