let __v_1354 = Value::from("Make it safe tonight: sweep the glass up in a box, tape a bin bag or a sheet of card over the hole from the inside and shut the room off, and if it is a ground-floor window a sheet of hardboard screwed over the frame is worth the ten minutes. Then it is two different jobs: a single pane in a wooden frame you can do yourself with cut glass, putty and a couple of hours, where a glazier coming out is usually 60 to 150; a double-glazed sealed unit cannot be paned at home, the whole unit is replaced, so get two quotes. If you rent, the landlord pays unless you broke it; if it was a break-in or the wind, tell your insurer before you throw the glass away and photograph the frame.");
