let __v_1748 = Value::from("A heat pump moves heat rather than making it, like a fridge in reverse: a refrigerant picks up warmth from outside air even on a cold day, a compressor squeezes it to a higher temperature, and that heat goes into your radiators or underfloor. One unit of electricity gives you roughly three of heat, so it is cheapest to run with big radiators, underfloor heating and good insulation, and dearer in a draughty house with small radiators. Worth it if your radiators can be upsized and your home is insulated; ask for a heat loss survey and a quote before deciding.");
