let __v_2310 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"washing powder\",\"soap powder\",\"laundry powder\",\"laundry detergent\",\"laundry liquid\",\"washing liquid\",\"washing capsules\",\"laundry capsules\",\"washing detergent\"]},\"A teaspoon of washing-up liquid or shampoo gets one load through: it will not foam the same and it is not for every week, but a wash now beats a sour load. A 30-wash box lasts about a month for two people, so keep a spare under the sink, and a tablespoon of powder is enough for a normal load.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"kitchen roll\",\"kitchen towel\",\"kitchen towels\",\"paper towel\",\"paper towels\",\"kitchen paper\"]},\"A tea towel and a pile of old cloths do the same job, and newspaper is better than either for glass and windows. Buy a four-pack and keep one roll back; a roll lasts about a week in a busy kitchen, and the blue shop towels are the ones worth the extra for grease.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tin foil\",\"foil\",\"aluminium foil\",\"silver foil\"]},\"Baking paper on a tray, and a lid or an upturned plate over a dish, cover most of what foil does; for the grill, oil the rack and slide a tray underneath. A 30cm roll lasts a couple of months, and a wide catering roll is cheaper by the metre if you use it for roasting.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cling film\",\"clingfilm\",\"plastic wrap\",\"saran wrap\",\"shrink wrap\"]},\"A plate on top of a bowl, foil, or a saucepan lid covers most things, a freezer bag does instead in the freezer, and a shower cap over a bowl is the trick that works in the fridge. Beeswax wraps are the reusable version and last about a year, so they pay for themselves.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dishwasher tablets\",\"dishwasher tablet\",\"dishwasher powder\",\"dishwasher salt\",\"rinse aid\"]},\"Two tablespoons of soda crystals on a hot empty cycle cleans the machine, and most of the UK has water soft enough to skip the salt for a week. A splash of white vinegar stands in for rinse aid, and half a tablet does a normal wash in a soft-water area.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"toilet roll\",\"toilet rolls\",\"loo roll\",\"toilet paper\",\"bog roll\"]},\"Kitchen roll or tissues will get you through a day, and neither belongs down the loo in a handful - paper and water are the only things that should go in. Two people use three or four rolls a week, so buy the big pack and keep one under the stairs.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bin bags\",\"bin bag\",\"bin liners\",\"bin liner\",\"rubbish bags\",\"black bags\"]},\"A carrier bag, or the bag out of a cereal box, lines a kitchen bin for a day: double it if the rubbish is heavy and keep food waste in its own bag so it cannot split. A roll of 20 lasts about two months, and the next size up holds a week of kitchen rubbish.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"washing up liquid\",\"washing-up liquid\",\"dish soap\",\"dishwashing liquid\",\"fairy liquid\"]},\"A squirt of hand soap or shampoo in hot water will do a sink of dishes, and a spoon of soda crystals cuts grease better than either; never put dishwasher tablets in a bowl of washing up. A 500ml bottle lasts about two months of daily washing up.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bleach\",\"toilet cleaner\",\"loo cleaner\",\"disinfectant\",\"harpic\",\"domestos\"]},\"A tablespoon of soda crystals left in the loo overnight and a scrub with the brush does the same job, and washing-up liquid with hot water does a basin or a floor. Never mix bleach with vinegar or with a limescale remover: the gas that comes off is what hurts people. Thin bleach is the cheap one - buy two litres at a time.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"shampoo\",\"shampoos\",\"conditioner\"]},\"A bar of soap washes hair for a few days, and a spoon of bicarbonate of soda stirred into a mug of warm water is the old stand-in; expect it to feel rough without conditioner. A 400ml bottle lasts about two months at three washes a week, so a spare is worth keeping.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"toothpaste\",\"tooth paste\"]},\"Brush with water alone for a day or two: it still lifts the film off the teeth and washes the sugar away, and keep flossing until you shop. A pea-sized amount means a 100ml tube lasts about two months at twice a day.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"soap\",\"hand soap\",\"bar soap\",\"handwash\",\"hand wash\"]},\"Washing-up liquid or shower gel does the job at a sink for a few days, and a spoon of soda crystals in warm water is the cheap hand wash. A bar lasts about a month in a busy bathroom, and bars work out cheaper than pumps per wash.\"]}]}")?;
