let __v_4527 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"ground rent\"]},\"Ground rent is the yearly charge a leaseholder pays the freeholder for the land the flat stands on, on top of the service charge: often £100 to £300, and now usually a fixed sum written into the lease. It is not the same as the service charge, which pays for the building, and a lease with ground rent that doubles every ten years is the one to argue about before you buy.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"my\",\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"increase\",\"doubled\",\"doubling\",\"demand\",\"arrears\",\"paying\",\"pay it\",\"not paying\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tenancy deposit\",\"deposit scheme\",\"deposit protection\"]},\"A tenancy deposit is the money you pay a landlord at the start to cover damage or unpaid rent, usually five weeks' rent, and it is not the landlord's to keep: in England and Wales it must be put in a government-backed protection scheme within 30 days and you get a certificate saying where. If it was not protected, or your landlord keeps it for wear and tear, you can claim up to three times the deposit.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"not paid back\",\"not returned\",\"withheld\",\"kept my\",\"claim\",\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"my landlord\",\"how much\",\"returned\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"reserve fund\",\"major works fund\",\"reserve funds\"]},\"A reserve fund - a sinking fund, in a block of flats - is money the leaseholders pay into each month so the big jobs of the next twenty years, a new roof or lifts or external paint, are already paid for when they come. It is separate from the service charge for this year's running costs, and the balance shows in the annual accounts, so check it before you buy a leasehold flat.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"my\",\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"start one\",\"set one up\",\"for a car\",\"house deposit\",\"savings\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"break clause\",\"breakclause\"]},\"A break clause is a term in a tenancy or a commercial lease that lets either side end it early, on a date and with notice written into the contract: you still pay the rent until that date, and the notice is often two months. Ask exactly how the notice has to be given, in writing, and diary the day two months before the break date.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"grammar\",\"sentence\",\"verb\",\"clause in\",\"relative clause\",\"subordinate\",\"my\",\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"can i leave\",\"exercise it\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"inventory\",\"check in report\",\"check-in report\"]},\"An inventory is the list of what was in the flat and what condition it was in when you moved in, with photos, and it is the document the deposit is judged against at the end. Check it against the flat on the day, write down anything missing or already damaged, date and sign it, and photograph any marks before you send it back.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"stock\",\"shop\",\"business\",\"warehouse\",\"my\",\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"do one\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"contents insurance\",\"contents cover\"]},\"Contents insurance covers the things in the home: furniture, clothes, a laptop, a bike if it is listed, the damage a leak or a fire does to them - where buildings insurance covers the structure itself, which is the landlord's job in a rented flat. Add up what it would cost to replace everything new, keep receipts for anything over a few hundred pounds, and check the single-item limit before you assume the bike is covered.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"my\",\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"claim\",\"not paying\",\"renew\",\"cancel\",\"cheapest\",\"compare\",\"do i need\"]}]}]}")?;
